                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2359</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-27T23:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1918,
                                11 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 28, 1.50 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My telegram of July 24, 5 p.m. A memorandum from the Foreign Office announces
                    that the Chinese Government consents that the Czecho-Slovak Army shall enjoy
                    unrestricted freedom in the use of the Chinese Eastern Railway.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
